{"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Benchmarks"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The benchmark suite measures the same workloads at several committed FirebladeECS revisions, such as a release tag against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main"},{"type":"text","text":". The workloads cover entity creation, destruction and lookup, adding and removing components, iterating families, system updates and component events. Revisions with value-type components run each workload on both the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"archetype"},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" storage (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), so a report also shows what the storage choice costs."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"How results are made trustworthy","anchor":"How-results-are-made-trustworthy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each revision is built once and measured in "},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" independent process replicates, interleaved in a seeded random order. The replicate is the unit of analysis: the centre value is the median of the replicate medians, with a distribution-free order-statistic 95% confidence interval. A speed-up against the baseline is the Hodges–Lehmann estimate with its exact confidence interval, tested with an exact Mann–Whitney test and adjusted across all comparisons of a report with Benjamini–Hochberg. A change counts as "},{"code":"faster","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"slower","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only when it is significant and clears the ±5% equivalence zone; an interval inside that zone is reported as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"equivalent"},{"type":"text","text":", anything else as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inconclusive"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Read and reproduce","anchor":"Read-and-reproduce"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest published report: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Reports are published for dedicated benchmark releases only; the page shows the newest."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The 2.0.0 report: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", the full suite with 10 replicates on both storages. Its source is committed as "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/BenchmarkReport.html","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The statistical design and workload parity notes: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/Methodology.md","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To measure revisions locally, pass comma-separated tags, branches or commit IDs. Results are saved under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/Results\/<UTC timestamp>\/"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh","code":["make benchmark-compare REFS=1.4.3,main:2.0.0 REPLICATES=10 BENCHMARK_FILTER='.*'","make benchmark-report RESULTS=\"Benchmarks\/Results\/<run>\/*.json\" REPORT_BASELINE=1.4.3"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without "},{"code":"BENCHMARK_FILTER","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only 16 entities of every workload plus ","type":"text"},{"code":"entity.create.no-entities","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (which only has 0 entities) run. ","type":"text"},{"code":"make benchmark-report","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" renders the single file ","type":"text"},{"code":"BenchmarkReport.html","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from saved results and never runs benchmarks. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/README.md"},{"type":"text","text":" for all options."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/SavingAndLoadingScenes":{"kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","title":"Saving and Loading Scenes","abstract":[{"text":"Store a whole ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" on disk and load it again with the same entities, components and entity identifiers.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/savingandloadingscenes"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","title":"FirebladeECS","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus."}],"title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"u